# Lumos - tools/bootstrap/sample-env / Deterministic sample environment.
# Author: dhar.abhishek.email@gmail.com
# Implements: TRS-REP-006, TRS-REP-004, TRS-REP-005
# ADRs: ADR-003
# Threading: n/a
#
# EVERY VALUE HERE IS A PLACEHOLDER. Nothing in this file is, was, or may ever
# become a real credential. Production signing material and service credentials
# live only in owner-controlled KMS/HSM and never in source or CI logs
# (TRS-REP-005, owner gate G-05). If you find yourself editing this file to add
# a real value, you are editing the wrong file: copy it to .env.local, which is
# git-ignored.
#
# "Deterministic" means: two developers who follow README.md get byte-identical
# behaviour from the checks WP-01 ships. Every value below is fixed, and none
# is derived from the host, the clock, or the network.
#
#   cp tools/bootstrap/sample-env/lumos.env.sample .env.local

# --- build variant (TRS-REP-004) --------------------------------------------
# One of: development, test, staging, production. The four variants separate
# endpoints, keys and logging behaviour; they are not interchangeable labels.
LUMOS_ENVIRONMENT=development

# --- backend shell ----------------------------------------------------------
# The WP-01 backend serves /healthz and nothing else. The port is fixed so the
# sample environment is reproducible, not because 8080 is normative.
LUMOS_BACKEND_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8080
LUMOS_LOG_LEVEL=debug

# Build provenance stamped into the artefact (TRS-REP-007). CI overrides these
# from git; the placeholders keep a local build self-describing rather than
# blank.
LUMOS_VERSION=0.0.0-dev
LUMOS_REVISION=0000000
LUMOS_BUILD_ENV=development

# --- admin console shell ----------------------------------------------------
LUMOS_ADMIN_ENVIRONMENT=development

# --- Android SDK ------------------------------------------------------------
# Set only if the SDK is not in the platform default location. The bootstrap
# script reports what it finds; it does not write this for you.
# ANDROID_SDK_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/Android/Sdk

# --- what is deliberately ABSENT --------------------------------------------
# No database URL, object-store credential, push certificate, APNs key, Play
# service account, signing keystore password, config-package signing key or
# venue API token appears here, and none may be added. Each of those is either
# owner-held (G-05) or introduced by the work package that first needs it, with
# its own secret-handling decision. A placeholder for a secret that does not
# yet exist teaches the wrong habit and gives a secret scanner nothing to
# distinguish from the real thing.
